module

public import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasiCoherentAlgebra
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Limits.HasLimits

/-! # Integral quasi-coherent algebras as directed colimits

Source: Stacks Project, Properties, Lemma 28.23.13, Tag 0817
(blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-integral-algebra-directed-colimit-finite).
-/

@[expose] public section

universe v

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

noncomputable section

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- An integral quasi-coherent algebra on a qcqs scheme is the directed colimit of
all its finite quasi-coherent subalgebras, and a directed colimit of finite,
finitely presented quasi-coherent algebras. Cocones are colimits in all algebra
sheaves, and their legs are the stated maps to the given algebra.
Source: Stacks Project, Properties, Tag 0817
(blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-integral-algebra-directed-colimit-finite).

Proof (the nine steps of the node):
1. For a subalgebra B of A, finite module generators also generate the algebra.
   Conversely, finite algebra generators are integral because A is integral, so
   lem-weil-pbc-finite-of-integral-generators (Algebra 02JJ) makes B finite.
2. Apply lem-weil-pbc-algebra-directed-colimit-finite-type (05JT). By Step 1 its
   collection is exactly the finite quasi-coherent subalgebras, proving (1).
3. Write the underlying module A as a directed colimit of finitely presented modules
   F_i by lem-weil-pbc-module-directed-colimit-finite-presentation (01PK).
   Form S_i = Sym(F_i), with compatible maps to A induced by F_i -> A, using
   lem-weil-pbc-quasi-coherent-symmetric-algebra. Their kernels J_i are quasi-coherent
   ideals, and their images A'_i are quasi-coherent subalgebras, by
   lem-weil-pbc-quasi-coherent-algebra-kernel-image-ideal. The transition maps on
   symmetric algebras carry J_i into J_i' because their composites to A agree.
4. On every affine open S_i is finitely generated as an algebra, by
   lem-weil-pbc-symmetric-algebra-finite-presentation. Its image A'_i is therefore
   of finite type and, by Step 1, finite.
5. Write each J_i as a directed colimit of finitely presented modules E_ik (01PK).
   Let I_ik be the ideal of S_i generated by the image of E_ik, and put
   A_ik = S_i / I_ik. Since I_ik lies in J_i there is an induced map A_ik -> A.
   Use lem-weil-pbc-quasi-coherent-algebra-kernel-image-ideal for these quotients.
   On affine opens E_ik is finitely generated and F_i finitely presented, by
   lem-weil-pbc-quasi-coherent-finite-type-affine. Thus the quotient has finitely
   many algebra generators and relations, by
   lem-weil-pbc-symmetric-algebra-finite-presentation.
6. Order pairs (i,k) by increase of i and containment of the transported ideals.
   Containment induces quotient maps, compatible with their maps to A; uniqueness
   of quotient factorizations gives the identity and composition laws.
   The order is reflexive and transitive. For two pairs choose a common later i'.
   Each transported E_ik -> J_i' factors through some E_i'k', by
   lem-weil-pbc-finite-presentation-hom-directed-colimit (01BS). A common upper
   bound for these two k' gives an upper bound for the original pairs. Nonemptiness
   follows from nonemptiness of the original directed systems.
7. Form the algebra-sheaf colimit using lem-weil-pbc-quasi-coherent-algebra-colimit.
   On an affine open every section of A comes from some F_i, hence from an A_ik;
   use lem-weil-pbc-quasi-coherent-module-colimit-affine-sections. Conversely a
   section represented in A_ik lifts to S_i. If its image in A vanishes, the lift
   belongs to J_i and comes from some E_ik'. It therefore vanishes in a common
   later quotient. Use lem-weil-pbc-filtered-colimit-algebras-elementwise and
   lem-weil-pbc-filtered-colimit-rings-zero. The map on affine sections is bijective;
   lem-weil-pbc-sheaf-morphism-on-basis identifies the colimit with A.
8. Fix i and choose a finite affine cover of X. On each member take finite module
   generators of F_i. Their images in A'_i satisfy monic polynomial relations by
   lem-weil-pbc-finite-algebra-is-integral. These finitely many relations belong to
   J_i and hence occur in sufficiently late E_ik, simultaneously on the finite cover.
   For all later k the images of the generators in A_ik satisfy the same relations.
   By lem-weil-pbc-finite-of-integral-generators each such affine section algebra is
   finite; lem-weil-pbc-quasi-coherent-finite-type-affine gives finiteness everywhere.
9. The pairs with k beyond these bounds are cofinal: increase k at fixed i.
   They are directed by taking an upper bound in the full system and increasing k
   once more. Restrict to them using lem-weil-pbc-colimit-initial-full-subcategory.
   Their algebras are finite by Step 8, finitely presented by Step 5, and have colimit
   A by Step 7. This proves (2), with compatibility inherited from the quotient maps.
-/
theorem integral_algebra_directed_colimit_finite
    (X : Scheme.{v}) [CompactSpace X] [QuasiSeparatedSpace X]
    (A : QuasiCoherentAlgebra X) (hA : A.obj.IsIntegral) :
    (Nonempty A.FiniteSubalgebras ∧
      IsDirected A.FiniteSubalgebras (· ≤ ·) ∧
      ∃ (c : Cocone A.finiteSubalgebraDiagram) (e : c.pt ≅ A.obj),
        (∀ B : A.FiniteSubalgebras, c.ι.app B ≫ e.hom = B.val.arrow) ∧
        Nonempty (IsColimit c)) ∧
    (∃ (I : Type v) (_ : Preorder I) (_ : Nonempty I) (_ : IsDirected I (· ≤ ·))
      (F : I ⥤ QuasiCoherentAlgebra X)
      (c : Cocone (F ⋙ (X.IsQuasiCoherentAlgebra).ι)) (e : c.pt ≅ A.obj),
      (∀ i : I, (F.obj i).obj.IsFinite ∧ (F.obj i).obj.IsFinitePresentation) ∧
      Nonempty (IsColimit c)) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
